course: dictionary
lesson: 1198
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it, which are its context. «The bath was full of bubbly foam.» Here bubbly means full of bubbles.
explain: «Mia is so bubbly that everyone in class wants to sit next to her.» Bubbly is not about bubbles here. Mia is lively, cheerful and full of energy. Ask: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word, and see if it still makes sense.
explain: In «Grown-ups raised a glass of bubbly at the wedding», bubbly is an informal word for champagne or another sparkling wine. The clues are the glass and the wedding. Here the word names a drink, so it is a noun.
explain: Context also helps with words from other languages. «"xīngfèn" means excited, the bubbly can't-sit-still feeling before a birthday, a trip or a festival.» The word bubbly tells you that excited feels full of energy.
fact: Bubbly is an adjective: bubbly, bubblier, bubbliest.
fact: «Bubbly» means full of bubbles, as in «bubbly water» or «a bubbly bath».
fact: «Bubbly» also means lively, cheerful and full of energy, as in «a bubbly personality».
fact: Informally, «bubbly» as a noun means champagne or another sparkling wine.
fact: Many words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is right.
exercise: «The lemonade was bubbly and fizzy.» What does bubbly mean here? | Sad and quiet | Lively and cheerful | *Full of bubbles | Made of wood
exercise: «Our new class helper is so bubbly that she makes everyone laugh.» What does bubbly mean here? | Full of bubbles | Angry and cold | Dirty and untidy | *Lively, cheerful and full of energy
exercise: At the wedding, Dad raised a glass of bubbly. What is bubbly in this sentence? | A bath full of foam | A happy child | A kind of cake | *Champagne or another sparkling wine
test: Find the meaning of bubbly in «He has a bubbly laugh that fills the room.» | Wet and cold | *Lively and cheerful | Hard to hear | Full of bubbles
test: Which sentence uses bubbly as a noun? | *They toasted with bubbly at New Year | Bubbly means cheerful | Aunt Jo is bubbly at parties | The bath is bubbly
exam: Which meaning of bubbly fits «The bubbly bath made the whole room smell of strawberries»? | Champagne or sparkling wine | Lively and cheerful | Very quiet | *Full of bubbles
